WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:04.760
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.080
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.360
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.620
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.440
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们制作终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:19.420
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会解析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:20.540
We're The Office Ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:28.780
I hope you're in a festive mood today because we're talking about Moroccan Christmas.
希望你今天心情不错，因为我们要聊的是“摩洛哥圣诞节”。

9
00:00:29.180 --> 00:00:35.960
So get out your Christmas plaid, but put away that nativity scene because Phyllis is going to throw you the party of a lifetime.
所以拿出你的圣诞格子衫，但把那个耶稣诞生场景收起来，因为菲利斯要为你举办一场终生难忘的派对。

10
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:37.000
She sure is.
她确实会。

11
00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:43.680
It's Season 5, Episode 11, written by Justin Spitzer and directed by Paul Feig.
这是第五季第11集，由贾斯汀·斯皮策编剧，保罗·费格执导。

12
00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:45.480
Here is your summary.
这是剧情梗概。

13
00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:57.420
As you said, Phyllis throws a Moroccan-themed Christmas party, which receives compliments from the majority of the group, but some serious contempt from Angela.
正如你所说，菲利斯举办了一场摩洛哥主题的圣诞派对，大多数人都称赞有加，但安吉拉却表现出极大的蔑视。

14
00:00:57.560 --> 00:00:58.640
Oh, she is not happy.
噢，她可不高兴了。

15
00:00:59.200 --> 00:01:03.360
Dwight runs a black market doll trade out of The Office.
德怀特在办公室里经营着黑市玩偶交易。

16
00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.120
And Meredith gets wasted and sets herself on fire.
梅雷迪思喝得烂醉，还把自己点着了。

17
00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.100
That's a doozy of a sentence.
这句话的信息量真大。

18
00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:11.780
It's quite a work party.
这真是一场特别的职场派对。

19
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:17.780
Michael decides to hold an intervention demanding Meredith get help for her alcoholism.
迈克尔决定举行一次干预行动，要求梅雷迪思为她的酗酒问题寻求帮助。

20
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:21.220
And then, talk about a doozy of a work party.
说到信息量大的职场派对，这绝对算一个。

21
00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:21.820
Ugh.
呃。

22
00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:26.600
Phyllis spills the beans about Angela and Dwight in front of everyone.
菲利斯在所有人面前泄露了安吉拉和德怀特的事。

23
00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:27.300
Everyone!
所有人！

24
00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:29.460
She announces it to the whole bullpen!
她向整个办公区宣布了这件事！

25
00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:30.500
Except Andy.
除了安迪。

26
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:32.040
Oh, Andy.
噢，安迪。

27
00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:32.940
Yeah.
是啊。

28
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:34.360
Andy in a sitar.
弹西塔琴的安迪。

29
00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:39.020
His goodbye as he's leaving broke my heart.
他离开时的告别让我心碎。

30
00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:39.980
We're getting ahead.
我们说远了。

31
00:01:40.120 --> 00:01:41.000
We're getting ahead.
我们说远了。

32
00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:41.700
We're getting ahead.
我们说远了。

33
00:01:41.720 --> 00:01:41.840
All right.
好吧。

34
00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:44.200
Fast fact number one.
第一个速览事实。

35
00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:48.860
This was the third Christmas-themed episode of The Office.
这是《办公室》的第三集圣诞主题剧集。

36
00:01:48.860 --> 00:01:49.760
Yes, it was.
没错，确实是。

37
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:52.860
Season five, but only three Christmas episodes.
虽然是第五季，但只有三集圣诞特辑。

38
00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:53.360
Why?
为什么？

39
00:01:53.820 --> 00:01:56.040
Well, the first season, we didn't have one.
嗯，第一季的时候我们没有拍。

40
00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:56.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

41
00:01:56.880 --> 00:02:00.260
And then, in season four, it was the writer's strike.
然后，第四季的时候碰上了编剧罢工。

42
00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:01.020
I know.
我知道。

43
00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.020
We missed a Christmas party.
我们错过了一场圣诞派对。

44
00:02:03.020 --> 00:02:06.980
It has been two years since we had a Christmas party on The Office.
距离我们在《办公室》里举办圣诞派对已经过去两年了。

45
00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:10.220
They were always some of my favorite episodes, so I was excited.
它们一直是我最喜欢的剧集之一，所以我很兴奋。

46
00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:11.000
Me too.
我也是。

47
00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:14.480
I liked them because they were majority group scenes.
我喜欢它们是因为它们大部分都是集体戏。

48
00:02:14.780 --> 00:02:15.300
Yes.
是的。

49
00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:17.140
We were all together all the time.
我们一直都在一起。

50
00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:19.460
It was like a whole episode of Conference Room.
就像整集都在会议室里一样。

51
00:02:19.820 --> 00:02:21.280
So, lots of bits.
所以，有很多琐事。

52
00:02:21.540 --> 00:02:22.000
Lots of bits.
很多琐事。

53
00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:22.520
Lots of laughing.
有很多欢声笑语。

54
00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:24.560
We would just have the best time.
我们当时真的玩得特别开心。

55
00:02:24.760 --> 00:02:26.020
We would get loopy.
我们当时都疯疯癫癫的。

56
00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:26.900
We would.
确实如此。

57
00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:27.900
But in the best way.
但那是种很棒的状态。

58
00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:30.340
Fast fact number two.
第二个冷知识。

59
00:02:30.960 --> 00:02:36.000
The inspiration for this episode, I was able to get in touch with writer Justin Spitzer.
关于这一集的灵感来源，我联系上了编剧贾斯汀·斯皮策。

60
00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:37.420
What'd Justin have to say?
贾斯汀怎么说？

61
00:02:37.580 --> 00:02:42.180
He told me that they had had these two ideas rolling around for a really long time.
他告诉我，他们脑子里一直酝酿着两个点子，已经很久了。

62
00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.340
The first one was the idea of a Moroccan Christmas.
第一个点子是关于摩洛哥圣诞节。

63
00:02:46.940 --> 00:02:53.140
They just loved the idea that Phyllis had thrown that amazing goodbye party for Toby.
他们特别喜欢菲利斯为托比举办的那场精彩告别派对的构思。

64
00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:53.700
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

65
00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.060
And that maybe the success had gone to her head a little bit.
而且觉得那次成功可能让她有点飘了。

66
00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.320
And she's going to go big.
她打算大干一场。

67
00:02:58.460 --> 00:02:59.180
Big theme.
大主题。

68
00:02:59.400 --> 00:02:59.840
Yes.
没错。

69
00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:02.940
They loved that this would piss Angela off.
他们很喜欢这个点子，因为这会让安吉拉气炸。

70
00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:03.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

71
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:06.280
So, this was like one card.
所以，这就像是一张卡片上的内容。

72
00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:06.940
Right.
对。

73
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.500
You know what the card probably said?
你知道那张卡片上可能写了什么吗？

74
00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:08.680
What?
什么？

75
00:03:08.740 --> 00:03:10.580
Phyllis happy Angela pissed.
菲利斯开心，安吉拉气炸。

76
00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:12.120
Christmas.
圣诞节。

77
00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:13.360
Question mark.
问号。

78
00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:15.960
Why is your character always so angry on Christmas?
为什么你的角色在圣诞节总是那么生气？

79
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:17.660
She's angry all the time.
她一直都很生气。

80
00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.520
But it really comes out at the holidays.
但在节日期间表现得尤为明显。

81
00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:21.260
She has levels of anger.
她的愤怒是有层级的。

82
00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:23.540
Sometimes she's like suspicious bitch.
有时她是那种多疑的贱人。

83
00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.980
Sometimes she's happy bitch.
有时她是那种开心的贱人。

84
00:03:25.440 --> 00:03:25.620
Yeah.
是啊。

85
00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:26.480
Sometimes she's sad bitch.
有时她是那种悲伤的贱人。

86
00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:27.360
Hmm.
嗯。

87
00:03:27.360 --> 00:03:29.620
And then Christmas bitch is a whole different bitch.
而圣诞节的贱人则是完全不同的一种贱人。

88
00:03:29.820 --> 00:03:30.500
Oh, boy.
天哪。

89
00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.720
Buckle in for Christmas bitch.
做好准备迎接圣诞节贱人吧。

90
00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:34.580
Okay.
好吧。

91
00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:39.700
So, the other card that they had on the wall for a really long time said Meredith Intervention.
所以，他们墙上挂了很久的另一张卡片写的是：梅雷迪思干预行动。

92
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:40.940
Oh, okay.
哦，原来如此。

93
00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.380
So, they decided to marry these two ideas.
于是，他们决定把这两个点子结合起来。

94
00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:49.280
Remember when they did like Michael has to fire someone on Halloween while we're all dressed up?
还记得他们拍过迈克尔必须在万圣节解雇某人，而我们都穿着戏服的那一集吗？

95
00:03:49.500 --> 00:03:49.700
Yeah.
记得。

96
00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:50.640
It's the same thing.
是一样的道理。

97
00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:51.140
Yes.
是的。

98
00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:51.820
Exactly.
没错。

99
00:03:52.660 --> 00:03:59.520
Justin said that a holiday party also seemed like a really good place for Meredith to drink too much and set her hair on fire.
贾斯汀说，节日派对似乎也是梅雷迪思喝多并烧着头发的好时机。

100
00:03:59.520 --> 00:04:03.000
Like, there could be this sort of rock-bottomy moment.
就像是，可以出现那种跌入谷底的时刻。

101
00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:03.440
Right.
没错。

102
00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:04.460
And it's an event.
而且这是一场盛事。

103
00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.080
It's like a big event and everyone's there to witness it.
就像一场大型活动，每个人都在现场见证。

104
00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:07.500
Yes.
是的。

105
00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:13.120
Fast fact number three, I have a talking head observation for this episode.
第三个冷知识，关于这一集，我有一个关于“访谈”镜头的发现。

106
00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.260
Oh, I'm so curious.
噢，我太好奇了。

107
00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:21.300
So, as you re-watch this episode, take a note of the talking heads.
所以，当你重温这一集时，留意一下那些访谈镜头。

108
00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:27.840
Almost all of them are filmed from different angles than we normally would.
几乎所有的镜头拍摄角度都和我们平时拍的不一样。

109
00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:34.200
I believe there's only one where someone's seated in the traditional chair with the kind of party through the blind.
我记得只有一个镜头是有人坐在传统的椅子上，背景是那种百叶窗。

110
00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:34.820
Right.
没错。

111
00:04:34.820 --> 00:04:35.200
Right.
没错。

112
00:04:35.360 --> 00:04:36.600
We're all over the office.
我们当时在办公室各处拍摄。

113
00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:37.960
All over the office.
办公室各处。

114
00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:42.860
So, this was not just because there was a party happening behind us.
所以，这不仅仅是因为我们身后正在举办派对。

115
00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:51.360
Justin said this was because they wanted to wait until they were in the editing room to place the talking heads throughout the episode.
贾斯汀说这是因为他们想等到剪辑室里，再决定把这些访谈镜头安插在这一集的什么位置。

116
00:04:51.520 --> 00:05:00.080
And they didn't want anything in the background to, like, in some way, mess up their ability to move these talking heads around.
他们不想让背景里的任何东西，以某种方式影响他们随意移动这些访谈镜头。

117
00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:03.760
Well, they had probably learned their lesson from that episode, Weight Loss.
嗯，他们大概是从“减肥”那一集吸取了教训。

118
00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:04.180
Yeah.
没错。

119
00:05:04.260 --> 00:05:11.560
Where they had to digitally, it's a hard word to say, they had to digitally change Ed's tie and shirt.
在那一集里，他们不得不——这个词很难念——他们不得不通过数字技术修改了艾德的领带和衬衫。

120
00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:11.940
Yeah.
没错。

121
00:05:11.940 --> 00:05:15.380
So, they kept moving the talking heads and what was happening behind them didn't match.
因为他们一直在移动访谈镜头，导致背景里发生的事情对不上。

122
00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:15.920
Yeah.
没错。

123
00:05:16.060 --> 00:05:20.060
So, you'll notice even Michael's talking heads, he is not seated at his desk.
所以你会注意到，连迈克尔的访谈镜头里，他都没有坐在办公桌前。

124
00:05:20.180 --> 00:05:30.340
He's standing in front of his desk and they purposely framed out the window behind him because timing-wise, they didn't know if it would be, like,
他是站在办公桌前的，而且他们特意避开了他身后的窗户，因为从时间安排上来说，他们不知道到时候会是，比如，

125
00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.600
still daytime or if it would be evening.
还是白天，或者是傍晚。

126
00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:37.260
So, they really tried to make all the talking heads as totally neutral as possible.
所以，他们真的尽量让所有的访谈镜头都保持绝对的中性。

127
00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:38.020
Smart.
聪明。

128
00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:38.640
Yeah.
没错。

129
00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.620
And it was kind of fun.
而且这还挺有趣的。

130
00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:44.660
After Justin told me that, I went back and re-watched the episode and it was totally true.
贾斯汀告诉我之后，我回去重看了这一集，发现确实如此。

131
00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:45.360
Yeah.
没错。

132
00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:50.060
I read the shooting draft and definitely things are moved all around.
我读了拍摄剧本，确实有很多地方被挪动了。

133
00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:52.160
So, it's good they did it.
所以，他们这么做是对的。

134
00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:52.480
Yeah.
没错。

135
00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:53.980
That's all I got.
这就是我所有的发现了。

136
00:05:53.980 --> 00:05:58.400
Well, before we get into this episode, I went digging in my digital clutter.
好吧，在进入这一集之前，我翻了翻我的电子文档。

137
00:05:58.700 --> 00:05:59.200
Okay.
好的。

138
00:05:59.660 --> 00:06:06.400
And I found an email from Paul Feig that on December 11th, 2008, he emailed the group, Jenna,
我找到了一封保罗·费格在2008年12月11日发给我们的邮件，珍娜，

139
00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:13.460
and invited us all to a Christmas taco party to watch the Moroccan Christmas episode at his house.
他邀请我们所有人去他家参加圣诞塔可派对，一起看“摩洛哥圣诞”那一集。

140
00:06:13.460 --> 00:06:14.120
Oh.
噢。

141
00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:22.960
And he said, I know, I know, Morocco and tacos make no sense, except they do kind of rhyme and we have a really great taco cart that we want to use.
他说，我知道，我知道，摩洛哥和塔可（墨西哥夹饼）完全不搭，但它们听起来有点押韵，而且我们有一个很棒的塔可餐车想用一下。

142
00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:29.820
And we all went over to his house December 11th, 2008, and watched Moroccan Christmas together.
于是我们都在2008年12月11日去了他家，一起看了“摩洛哥圣诞”。

143
00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:39.380
Aw, I love that you brought that up because Paul and Lori Feig used to host so many viewing parties at their house and they were just the most wonderful hosts.
噢，我很高兴你提到了这个，因为保罗和洛里·费格过去常在他们家举办观影派对，他们真是最棒的主人。

144
00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:44.260
And I'll never forget, he had that screen that would come down from the ceiling.
我永远不会忘记，他有一个会从天花板降下来的屏幕。

145
00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.880
So, he had like a very normal looking living room.
所以，他的客厅看起来非常普通。

146
00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:47.180
Yeah.
没错。

147
00:06:47.620 --> 00:06:49.820
Cozy, like a place you'd read books.
很温馨，就像那种你会读书的地方。

148
00:06:49.820 --> 00:06:52.420
I believe there was like a green leather chair.
我记得好像有一把绿色皮椅子。

149
00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:52.840
Oh, yeah.
噢，没错。

150
00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:55.760
There was like cozy chairs with like a blanket draped over it.
还有那种舒适的椅子，上面还搭着毯子。

151
00:06:55.760 --> 00:07:04.500
So cozy, and then all of a sudden when it was time to watch the show, the screen would come down out of the ceiling and it would turn into this amazing viewing experience.
非常舒适，然后突然间，当到了看节目的时候，屏幕就会从天花板上降下来，变成一种令人惊叹的观影体验。

152
00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:06.760
I thought, these guys are doing it right.
我想，这些人真是做对了。

153
00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:07.780
