Listen, every once in a while.
听着，偶尔为之嘛。

943
00:41:28.430 --> 00:41:30.790
You're going to lick a piece of granola bar off your shirt.
你居然会把衬衫上的燕麦棒碎屑舔掉。

944
00:41:30.790 --> 00:41:31.990
You know what else I'm going to do sometimes?
你知道我有时还会干什么吗？

945
00:41:32.170 --> 00:41:34.450
Sometimes the salad dressing is so good.
有时候沙拉酱太好吃了。

946
00:41:34.450 --> 00:41:35.490
I lick the plate.
我会舔盘子。

947
00:41:35.950 --> 00:41:36.250
Okay.
好吧。

948
00:41:36.250 --> 00:41:40.750
I'm here for licking the plate, but you just ate a piece of granola off your t-shirt.
舔盘子我能理解，但你刚才可是从T恤上吃了一块燕麦棒。

949
00:41:40.750 --> 00:41:47.170
You lifted your shirt up towards you so you could eat that tiny piece of granola.
你把衬衫撩起来凑近嘴边，就为了吃那一点点燕麦碎。

950
00:41:47.590 --> 00:41:49.190
Because I'm a classy lady.
因为我是位优雅的女士。

951
00:41:49.370 --> 00:41:50.210
You are classy.
你很有格调。

952
00:41:50.390 --> 00:41:50.910
And you know what?
而且你知道吗？

953
00:41:51.010 --> 00:41:51.970
You do not waste.
你从不浪费。

954
00:41:52.130 --> 00:41:53.110
And that I respect.
这一点我很敬佩。

955
00:41:53.370 --> 00:41:53.810
Thank you.
谢谢。

956
00:41:54.330 --> 00:41:54.750
Okay.
好的。

957
00:41:54.950 --> 00:42:02.370
As I was saying, Oscar, Jim, Michael, and Stanley try to set a date for something.
正如我刚才所说，奥斯卡、吉姆、迈克尔和斯坦利试图定个时间做某事。

958
00:42:02.370 --> 00:42:04.510
We don't know what they're talking about.
我们不知道他们在谈论什么。

959
00:42:04.930 --> 00:42:07.890
They're trying to agree on a time to do something.
他们正试图商定一个时间去做某事。

960
00:42:08.490 --> 00:42:09.370
Nothing's working.
怎么都定不下来。

961
00:42:09.370 --> 00:42:13.830
We do learn that Michael goes to the dentist every month.
我们确实了解到迈克尔每个月都要去看牙医。

962
00:42:14.070 --> 00:42:15.690
Well, because of his soft teeth.
嗯，因为他的牙齿很软。

963
00:42:15.890 --> 00:42:16.850
Every month.
每个月。

964
00:42:16.850 --> 00:42:18.730
We established that in Dinner Party.
我们在《晚宴》那一集里就确定了这一点。

965
00:42:18.990 --> 00:42:20.790
I feel like he talks their ear off.
我觉得他肯定在那儿喋喋不休。

966
00:42:20.930 --> 00:42:25.590
I feel like there's like a dental hygienist that he just talks their ear off.
我觉得肯定有个牙科保健员被他烦得不行。

967
00:42:25.910 --> 00:42:27.690
What do you do for soft teeth?
牙齿软该怎么办？

968
00:42:27.850 --> 00:42:28.270
You know what?
你知道吗？

969
00:42:28.370 --> 00:42:30.190
I'm going to ask my dentist the next time I'm there.
下次去看牙医时我要问问他。

970
00:42:30.310 --> 00:42:31.350
He's a fan of the show.
他是我们节目的粉丝。

971
00:42:31.530 --> 00:42:33.430
He's also a bread maker.
他还是个面包师。

972
00:42:33.850 --> 00:42:35.830
And he gave me his sourdough discard.
他给了我他的酸种面团废弃物。

973
00:42:36.190 --> 00:42:39.110
And it is fantastic sourdough discard.
那可是非常棒的酸种面团废弃物。

974
00:42:39.110 --> 00:42:39.790
Wow.
哇。

975
00:42:40.270 --> 00:42:40.950
Great dentiSt.
很棒的牙医。

976
00:42:41.310 --> 00:42:41.590
Okay.
好的。

977
00:42:41.850 --> 00:42:42.310
Great baker.
很棒的面包师。

978
00:42:42.430 --> 00:42:43.870
I'm going to ask him about soft teeth.
我要问问他关于牙齿软的问题。

979
00:42:44.030 --> 00:42:44.450
Stay tuned.
敬请期待。

980
00:42:44.710 --> 00:42:45.610
Baker and a dentiSt.
既是面包师又是牙医。

981
00:42:46.090 --> 00:42:52.310
Listen, they also can't do it on Groundhog Day because Michael, he celebrates privately.
听着，他们也不能在土拨鼠日那天聚会，因为迈克尔要私下庆祝。

982
00:42:53.730 --> 00:42:58.190
Some fans asked Justin in an interview once, what is it that Michael's doing?
有粉丝曾在采访中问贾斯汀，迈克尔到底在做什么？

983
00:42:58.730 --> 00:43:02.190
And he said, I imagine he just watches Groundhog Day all day.
他说，我想他应该就是整天都在看《土拨鼠之日》。

984
00:43:02.650 --> 00:43:03.250
The movie.
那部电影。

985
00:43:03.450 --> 00:43:03.990
He watches the movie.
他在看那部电影。

986
00:43:03.990 --> 00:43:08.890
And I also think he watches to see if Punxsutawney, is it Punxsutawney?
而且我还觉得他在看普苏塔尼，是叫普苏塔尼吗？

987
00:43:09.070 --> 00:43:09.450
Phil?
菲尔？

988
00:43:09.690 --> 00:43:10.130
Yeah.
对。

989
00:43:10.430 --> 00:43:12.610
I think he watches to see if Phil sees his shadow.
我想他在看菲尔有没有看到自己的影子。

990
00:43:12.730 --> 00:43:14.150
I think he watches the whole broadcaSt.
我想他会看整个直播。

991
00:43:14.470 --> 00:43:14.850
It's a big event.
那可是件大事。

992
00:43:15.110 --> 00:43:16.250
Maybe he goes.
也许他会去现场。

993
00:43:16.570 --> 00:43:17.250
He's busy.
他很忙。

994
00:43:17.370 --> 00:43:18.070
That's what we know.
这就是我们所知道的。

995
00:43:18.150 --> 00:43:18.290
Yeah.
是的。

996
00:43:18.290 --> 00:43:24.370
In the end, they decide today is the day and what they're planning is an intervention.
最后，他们决定就是今天，而他们计划的是一场干预行动。

997
00:43:24.730 --> 00:43:28.070
Christmas Eve, office party, intervention.
平安夜，办公室派对，干预行动。

998
00:43:28.070 --> 00:43:35.710
Listen, if I had to explain what an intervention is, it's like a surprise party for people who
听着，如果非要解释什么是干预行动，它就像是为那些

999
00:43:35.710 --> 00:43:36.430
have addictions.
有瘾的人举办的惊喜派对。

1000
00:43:36.430 --> 00:43:40.910
And what you do is you make them feel badly about themselves, so they stop.
你要做的就是让他们对自己感到羞愧，这样他们就会戒掉。

1001
00:43:41.210 --> 00:43:42.090
Michael Scott.
迈克尔·斯科特。

1002
00:43:42.290 --> 00:43:43.130
Right there, guys.
就在那儿，伙计们。

1003
00:43:43.190 --> 00:43:43.970
Per Michael Scott.
按照迈克尔·斯科特的意思。

1004
00:43:44.050 --> 00:43:46.910
That was the talking head that made it into the show.
那是最终被剪进正片里的访谈片段。

1005
00:43:47.090 --> 00:43:52.030
Here is an alt that got deleted and it cracked me up.
这里有一个被删减的备选片段，把我逗乐了。

1006
00:43:52.210 --> 00:43:54.910
We're going to call this Responsibilitini, guys.
我们要管这个叫“责任马提尼”，伙计们。

1007
00:43:55.590 --> 00:43:57.570
It takes a lot of courage.
这需要很大的勇气。

1008
00:43:58.070 --> 00:43:59.190
To admit you are right.
承认你是对的。

1009
00:44:00.790 --> 00:44:04.570
And talking about my strengths has always been one of my strengths.
而且谈论我的长处一直以来都是我的长处之一。

1010
00:44:04.830 --> 00:44:05.730
And I am right.
而且我是对的。

1011
00:44:06.310 --> 00:44:07.390
Meredith needs help.
梅雷迪思需要帮助。

1012
00:44:08.070 --> 00:44:10.970
She needs help like an alcoholic needs a drink.
她需要帮助，就像酒鬼需要喝酒一样。

1013
00:44:11.410 --> 00:44:15.070
And she's about to get a big shot of Michael Scott.
她马上就要迎来一大杯迈克尔·斯科特了。

1014
00:44:15.610 --> 00:44:17.830
Straight up on the rocks with ice.
纯饮，加冰。

1015
00:44:18.130 --> 00:44:18.670
No chaser.
不加任何配料。

1016
00:44:19.310 --> 00:44:21.270
I call it a Responsibilitini.
我管它叫“责任马提尼”。

1017
00:44:22.810 --> 00:44:25.370
Shaken with lemon, twist of lime.
摇匀，加柠檬，再加一点青柠。

1018
00:44:27.130 --> 00:44:27.730
Okay.
好的。

1019
00:44:28.350 --> 00:44:28.790
Okay.
好的。

1020
00:44:29.630 --> 00:44:32.650
We've played a lot of talking heads that didn't make it.
我们播放了很多没能进入正片的访谈片段。

1021
00:44:32.790 --> 00:44:33.050
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1022
00:44:33.310 --> 00:44:35.510
A lot of scenes that didn't make it in the show.
还有很多没能进入正片的场景。

1023
00:44:35.610 --> 00:44:35.910
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1024
00:44:36.370 --> 00:44:37.650
This is the biggest tragedy.
这是最大的悲剧。

1025
00:44:39.330 --> 00:44:40.210
A Responsibilitini!
责任马提尼！

1026
00:44:40.470 --> 00:44:41.770
Everything about that was gold.
那段话简直是金句。

1027
00:44:42.110 --> 00:44:43.790
I could listen to it five times.
我可以听上五遍。

1028
00:44:44.010 --> 00:44:44.510
I know!
我知道！

1029
00:44:44.790 --> 00:44:46.670
I was like, I have to play it.
我当时就想，我一定要放出来。

1030
00:44:46.750 --> 00:44:47.610
This is gold.
这简直是金句。

1031
00:44:47.610 --> 00:44:56.750
That was like on the level of Dwight's whole speech about stealing the ball from Tiffany's and going to all the countries and all that.
那简直和德怀特关于从蒂芙尼偷球、去各个国家旅行的那整段演讲是一个级别的。

1032
00:44:57.050 --> 00:44:57.890
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1033
00:44:58.090 --> 00:44:58.930
It was so good.
太棒了。

1034
00:44:59.430 --> 00:45:01.250
You're going to get a big shot of Michael Scott.
你马上就要迎来一大杯迈克尔·斯科特了。

1035
00:45:01.430 --> 00:45:01.770
Oh.
噢。

1036
00:45:01.770 --> 00:45:03.610
Oh, shaken, not stirred.
噢，要摇匀的，不要搅拌的。

1037
00:45:04.690 --> 00:45:05.170
Responsibilitini!
责任马提尼！

1038
00:45:05.730 --> 00:45:06.550
That's incredible.
太不可思议了。

1039
00:45:07.090 --> 00:45:09.450
Well, we're all going to circle up on the floor now.
好了，我们现在都要在地板上围成一圈了。

1040
00:45:09.730 --> 00:45:10.790
Not Angela, though.
不过安吉拉除外。

1041
00:45:10.950 --> 00:45:12.370
Phyllis has other plans for you.
菲利斯为你准备了别的计划。

1042
00:45:13.490 --> 00:45:15.010
It involves a hairnet.
需要戴发网。

1043
00:45:15.550 --> 00:45:16.030
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1044
00:45:16.770 --> 00:45:17.750
Lots of fanning.
还要不停地扇风。

1045
00:45:17.970 --> 00:45:19.030
Got to fan some pitas.
得给皮塔饼扇风。

1046
00:45:19.150 --> 00:45:20.310
Got to toast them on both sides.
得把两面都烤一下。

1047
00:45:20.430 --> 00:45:21.630
Got to fan napkins.
还得给餐巾扇风。

1048
00:45:21.890 --> 00:45:22.050
Yeah.
是啊。

1049
00:45:22.590 --> 00:45:23.830
And off to the kitchen I go.
那我就去厨房了。

1050
00:45:24.470 --> 00:45:30.750
Meanwhile, the rest of us sit on the floor and engage in a real uncomfortable intervention of Meredith.
与此同时，我们剩下的人坐在地板上，对梅雷迪思进行一场真正尴尬的干预治疗。

1051
00:45:31.230 --> 00:45:34.090
I don't know how you guys got through the scene without laughing.
我不知道你们是怎么忍住没笑场拍完那场戏的。

1052
00:45:34.390 --> 00:45:37.010
I remember two things happening during this week.
我记得这周发生了两件事。

1053
00:45:37.170 --> 00:45:39.990
One, I was bummed because I was in the kitchen by myself.
第一，我当时挺郁闷的，因为我一个人待在厨房里。

1054
00:45:40.130 --> 00:45:40.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1055
00:45:40.290 --> 00:45:43.130
And I had to enter in during the scene.
而且我得在那场戏中间走进去。

1056
00:45:43.270 --> 00:45:44.590
So it's not like I had to be there.
所以我其实没必要一直待在那儿。

1057
00:45:44.850 --> 00:45:46.130
Do you remember this?
你还记得吗？

1058
00:45:46.390 --> 00:45:58.310
Because Justin reminded me of this, and I had forgotten it, which was that Paul Feig insisted on shooting the entire intervention scene from top to bottom without cutting,
因为贾斯汀提醒了我，我都快忘了，保罗·费格坚持要从头到尾一镜到底地拍完那场干预戏，中间不剪辑，

1059
00:45:58.310 --> 00:46:00.770
and every take was about eight minutes long.
每一条都要拍八分钟左右。

1060
00:46:00.990 --> 00:46:01.410
Yes.
没错。

1061
00:46:01.610 --> 00:46:04.670
So I would be in the kitchen, like, with a magazine.
所以我当时就待在厨房里，拿着本杂志。

1062
00:46:04.670 --> 00:46:11.370
I actually, on the DVD commentary, I said I brought a magazine back there eventually because I was back there so long.
其实我在DVD评论音轨里说过，后来我带了本杂志进去，因为我在后面待的时间太长了。

1063
00:46:11.510 --> 00:46:15.810
And then they would cue me, and then I would walk in, then I'd have to go back.
然后他们会给我信号，我就走进去，演完还得退回去。

1064
00:46:16.150 --> 00:46:17.030
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

1065
00:46:17.190 --> 00:46:17.810
So crazy.
太疯狂了。

1066
00:46:18.030 --> 00:46:19.710
I remember my legs fell asleep.
我记得我的腿都坐麻了。

1067
00:46:20.010 --> 00:46:24.950
It's very hard to sit on the floor in a pencil skirt and pantyhose.
穿着包臀裙和连裤袜坐在地板上真的很难受。

1068
00:46:24.950 --> 00:46:27.050
Well, you had to do an odd cross.
嗯，你当时还得摆出一个奇怪的坐姿。

1069
00:46:27.250 --> 00:46:34.130
You had to do that one foot under the other, and at nine minutes, 46 seconds, there's a real good Pam pantyhose catch.
你得把一只脚压在另一只脚下面，在九分四十六秒的时候，能清楚地看到帕姆的连裤袜勾丝了。

1070
00:46:34.710 --> 00:46:35.230
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

1071
00:46:35.430 --> 00:46:36.670
I can see your pantyhose.
我能看到你的连裤袜。

1072
00:46:36.990 --> 00:46:38.170
I don't doubt it.
我一点也不怀疑。

1073
00:46:38.370 --> 00:46:39.750
You have pantyhose toes.
你有连裤袜脚趾。

1074
00:46:40.050 --> 00:46:46.190
I remember trying to figure out, because, you know, once you pick the way you're sitting, you have to sit like that.
我记得当时在想，因为你知道，一旦选定了坐姿，就得一直保持那个姿势。

1075
00:46:46.330 --> 00:46:48.830
You can't shift and move or change your position.
你不能挪动、调整或者改变姿势。

1076
00:46:48.830 --> 00:46:50.730
Because it has to match, you guys.
因为必须得连戏，各位。

1077
00:46:50.890 --> 00:46:52.790
So however you sit, that's it.
所以无论你怎么坐，就得一直那样。

1078
00:46:52.950 --> 00:46:55.350
So Mindy laying on her stomach like that.
所以明迪那样趴在地上。

1079
00:46:55.430 --> 00:46:56.530
Oh, I was so jealous.
哦，我当时真是羡慕死了。

1080
00:46:56.710 --> 00:46:57.630
Which I took a picture of.
我还拍了张照片。

1081
00:46:57.830 --> 00:47:00.490
I was jealous at first, but then you know her back started to ache.
起初我很羡慕，但后来你知道，她的背开始疼了。

1082
00:47:00.590 --> 00:47:03.210
It had to, because that's like doing a, what is that, the cow?
肯定会疼的，因为那就像是在做，那个叫什么来着，牛式？

1083
00:47:03.390 --> 00:47:04.150
No, it's not a cow.
不，不是牛式。

1084
00:47:04.570 --> 00:47:05.450
It's the snake.
是眼镜蛇式。

1085
00:47:05.630 --> 00:47:06.510
It's a yoga thing.
那是瑜伽动作。

1086
00:47:06.630 --> 00:47:07.050
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1087
00:47:07.170 --> 00:47:08.570
What's that yoga pose called?
那个瑜伽动作叫什么来着？

1088
00:47:08.830 --> 00:47:11.050
Were you, you arch your back up?
就是你把背拱起来那个？

1089
00:47:11.050 --> 00:47:11.170
The cobra.
眼镜蛇式。

1090
00:47:11.330 --> 00:47:11.650
Cobra!
眼镜蛇！

1091
00:47:12.450 --> 00:47:13.290
I knew it.
我就知道。

1092
00:47:13.430 --> 00:47:14.890
I don't know why that was so exciting.
我不知道为什么这事儿让我这么兴奋。

1093
00:47:14.890 --> 00:47:19.150
But just recalling any information at my age just gets me real amped up.
但以我这个年纪，能回想起任何信息都会让我特别激动。

1094
00:47:19.510 --> 00:47:21.630
So she had to do a mini cobra all day.
所以她得整天保持一个迷你眼镜蛇式的姿势。

1095
00:47:21.870 --> 00:47:26.010
You had to sit with the one foot under your butt, one foot extended.
你得一只脚压在屁股下面，另一只脚伸直。

1096
00:47:26.190 --> 00:47:26.430
Yep.
没错。

1097
00:47:26.570 --> 00:47:27.210
I know.
我知道。

1098
00:47:27.330 --> 00:47:30.050
And I do remember that we went around.
我确实记得我们轮流来。

1099
00:47:30.050 --> 00:47:32.330
And, you know, I was mostly reactions.
而且，你知道，我大部分时间都在做反应。

1100
00:47:32.330 --> 00:47:34.570
I don't think I had any lines in this scene.
我觉得我在那场戏里一句台词都没有。

1101
00:47:34.570 --> 00:47:36.490
It was very hard not to laugh.
忍住不笑真的很难。

1102
00:47:36.670 --> 00:47:43.030
It was very hard not to laugh when Creed says that he can get a fire permit in a couple hours.
当克里德说他能在几个小时内搞到消防许可证时，忍住不笑真的很难。

1103
00:47:43.830 --> 00:47:45.130
It was pretty amazing.
那真是太绝了。

1104
00:47:45.690 --> 00:47:51.550
We talked on the DVD commentary about Creed's outfit and what he's wearing in this scene.
我们在DVD评论音轨里聊过克里德的装扮，以及他在这一幕里穿的衣服。

1105
00:47:51.710 --> 00:47:54.070
He actually wore something similar to an award show.
他其实在颁奖典礼上穿过类似的衣服。

1106
00:47:54.270 --> 00:47:54.610
Do you remember?
你还记得吗？

1107
00:47:54.730 --> 00:47:56.050
He wore the long white.
他穿了那件长款白色的。

1108
00:47:56.610 --> 00:47:57.910
I don't remember this.
我不记得这个了。

1109
00:47:57.910 --> 00:48:01.410
This is very much sort of his outfit is something Creed would actually wear.
这确实很像克里德本人会穿的衣服。

1110
00:48:01.550 --> 00:48:02.650
And he looks fantastic.
而且他看起来棒极了。

1111
00:48:02.990 --> 00:48:04.990
There is a delicious Andy talking head.
安迪有一段非常精彩的访谈片段。

1112
00:48:05.170 --> 00:48:09.110
I feel like we all knew this guy in college, the guy that would chug a fifth of SoCo.
我觉得我们在大学里都认识这种人，那种能一口气灌下一瓶五分之一加仑南方舒适酒的人。

1113
00:48:09.570 --> 00:48:09.930
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

1114
00:48:11.270 --> 00:48:12.230
Boot, rally.
喝干，再来。

1115
00:48:12.230 --> 00:48:14.270
How many nicknames does he have, by the way?
顺便问一下，他到底有多少个绰号？

1116
00:48:14.270 --> 00:48:16.830
He's puke, he's ace, and he's buzz.
他叫“呕吐”，叫“王牌”，还叫“嗡嗡”。

1117
00:48:17.110 --> 00:48:19.210
Did he get straight A's or straight B's?
他是拿全A还是全B？

1118
00:48:19.270 --> 00:48:19.870
We're not sure.
我们不确定。

1119
00:48:20.290 --> 00:48:21.750
He got straight B's.
他拿的是全B。

1120
00:48:21.910 --> 00:48:23.430
Yeah, but he aced everything.
是啊，但他每门课都拿了满分。

1121
00:48:23.630 --> 00:48:23.850
Yeah.
没错。

1122
00:48:24.310 --> 00:48:31.150
Well, surprise, surprise, this intervention does not result in Meredith deciding to go to rehab.
好吧，不出所料，这次干预并没有让梅雷迪思决定去戒酒。

1123
00:48:31.530 --> 00:48:33.870
Michael's clearly not qualified to do this.
迈克尔显然没有资格做这件事。

1124
00:48:33.970 --> 00:48:35.150
And Toby's going to call it.
而且托比打算叫停了。

1125
00:48:35.290 --> 00:48:36.070
He's like, you know what?
他就像是说，你知道吗？

1126
00:48:36.170 --> 00:48:37.530
We're going to stop this.
我们要结束这一切了。

1127
00:48:37.530 --> 00:48:45.010
I do have to point out one of my favorite moments when Kevin offers his way that her drinking affected him.
我必须指出我最喜欢的时刻之一，就是凯文说出她的酗酒对他造成的影响时。

1128
00:48:45.210 --> 00:48:46.510
He got to go to the movies.
他能去看电影了。

1129
00:48:46.730 --> 00:48:48.310
By the way, thank you, he says.
顺便说一句，谢谢你，他是这么说的。

1130
00:48:48.570 --> 00:48:48.710
Yeah.
是啊。

1131
00:48:48.830 --> 00:48:50.250
Michael's like, you're not getting it.
迈克尔就像是说，你根本没明白。

1132
00:48:50.870 --> 00:48:51.750
But you're right.
但你说得对。

1133
00:48:51.930 --> 00:48:53.810
Michael is not trained to do this.
迈克尔没有受过这方面的训练。

1134
00:48:54.210 --> 00:48:57.170
You know, a trained interventioniSt.
你知道，专业的干预师。

1135
00:48:57.170 --> 00:48:59.030
This is a job in real life.
在现实生活中，这是一份职业。

1136
00:48:59.190 --> 00:49:00.310
People train for this.
人们为此接受过专门训练。

1137
00:49:00.810 --> 00:49:06.330
Kate had a whole speech that was in the script as Meredith, where she just addresses the group.
凯特作为梅雷迪思，剧本里有一整段台词，她直接对大家发表了讲话。

1138
00:49:06.410 --> 00:49:08.630
And she's like, listen, I'm bored.
她说，听着，我很无聊。

1139
00:49:08.690 --> 00:49:09.770
You're boring.
你们很无聊。

1140
00:49:09.790 --> 00:49:10.930
She said to Michael.
她对迈克尔说。

1141
00:49:11.090 --> 00:49:11.930
And he goes, hey.
然后他说，嘿。

1142
00:49:12.150 --> 00:49:13.490
And she was like, you know what?
她说，你知道吗？

1143
00:49:13.590 --> 00:49:14.570
I drink because I'm bored.
我喝酒是因为我无聊。

1144
00:49:14.730 --> 00:49:15.970
Try to be more interesting.
试着变得有趣一点吧。

1145
00:49:16.390 --> 00:49:17.190
Oh, my God.
天哪。

1146
00:49:17.190 --> 00:49:18.990
And she's like, who else is bored here?
然后她说，这里还有谁觉得无聊？

1147
00:49:19.090 --> 00:49:21.010
And like, everyone raises their hand.
结果每个人都举起了手。

1148
00:49:21.130 --> 00:49:23.310
She like hijacks the meeting from Michael, right?
她就像是从迈克尔手里抢过了会议的主导权，对吧？

1149
00:49:23.310 --> 00:49:26.330
And then she's like, we all do things to cope.
然后她说，我们每个人都有应对压力的方式。

1150
00:49:26.330 --> 00:49:27.650
So I drink when I'm bored.
所以我无聊的时候就喝酒。

1151
00:49:27.770 --> 00:49:29.250
And then she goes around the room.
然后她绕着房间走了一圈。

1152
00:49:29.370 --> 00:49:31.330
She goes, you all have coping mechanisMs.
她说，你们都有应对机制。

1153
00:49:31.370 --> 00:49:32.070
You eat.
你们吃东西。

1154
00:49:32.150 --> 00:49:32.630
You eat.
你们吃东西。

1155
00:49:32.770 --> 00:49:33.210
You eat.
你们吃东西。

1156
00:49:33.410 --> 00:49:34.250
You shop.
你们购物。

1157
00:49:34.450 --> 00:49:35.970
You confuse Dwight.
你们让德怀特感到困惑。

1158
00:49:36.650 --> 00:49:37.670
And then she's like.
然后她就说。

1159
00:49:37.910 --> 00:49:38.490
Who confuses Dwight, Jim?
吉姆，谁让德怀特感到困惑了？

1160
00:49:38.590 --> 00:49:38.990
Me.
我。

1161
00:49:39.170 --> 00:49:39.550
No, me.
不，是我。

1162
00:49:39.650 --> 00:49:40.170
Oh, OK.
哦，好吧。

1163
00:49:40.510 --> 00:49:42.290
And then she like points at Stanley.
然后她指着斯坦利。

1164
00:49:42.390 --> 00:49:43.190
And she's like, you eat.
她说，你吃东西。

1165
00:49:43.270 --> 00:49:46.750
And then Stanley has a talking head where he's like, I do eat when I'm bored.
然后斯坦利有个采访镜头，他说，我无聊的时候确实会吃东西。

1166
00:49:46.790 --> 00:49:48.130
But I also drink.
但我也会喝酒。

1167
00:49:48.450 --> 00:49:50.770
And I drink a lot more than Meredith.
而且我喝得比梅雷迪思多得多。

1168
00:49:50.970 --> 00:49:52.090
I just don't do it at work.
我只是不在工作时喝。

1169
00:49:52.090 --> 00:49:53.190
And I keep my clothes on.
而且我不会脱衣服。

1170
00:49:54.150 --> 00:49:55.970
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

1171
00:49:56.230 --> 00:49:56.510
Yes.
是的。

1172
00:49:56.650 --> 00:49:58.210
This scene was way bigger.
这一幕原本要长得多。

1173
00:49:58.870 --> 00:50:00.570
Oh, wow.
哇哦。

1174
00:50:01.290 --> 00:50:06.070
Michael is going to take Meredith into his office where they're going to talk for 45 minutes.
迈克尔要把梅雷迪思带进办公室，他们要在里面谈45分钟。

1175
00:50:06.670 --> 00:50:07.550
45 minutes.
45分钟。

1176
00:50:08.290 --> 00:50:13.190
And in the meantime, Angela is going to plead with Phyllis.
与此同时，安吉拉要向菲利斯求情。

1177
00:50:13.390 --> 00:50:15.570
Please, can I stop cutting the PETA?
求你了，我能别再剪那个善待动物组织（PETA）的传单了吗？

1178
00:50:15.850 --> 00:50:17.890
Do I really have to wear the hairnet?
我真的非得戴发网吗？

1179
00:50:18.230 --> 00:50:19.410
Have mercy.
发发慈悲吧。

1180
00:50:19.630 --> 00:50:20.970
It's the season of mercy.
现在是慈悲的季节。

1181
00:50:21.510 --> 00:50:22.830
Phyllis is no.
菲利斯说不行。

1182
00:50:22.830 --> 00:50:23.410
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1183
00:50:23.790 --> 00:50:24.170
No.
不行。

1184
00:50:24.490 --> 00:50:26.230
I have a thing I want to point out.
我有个细节想指出。

1185
00:50:26.470 --> 00:50:32.210
At 13 minutes, 35 seconds, Phyllis is telling Stanley about the Moroccan food they're eating.
在13分35秒时，菲利斯正在跟斯坦利说他们吃的摩洛哥食物。

1186
00:50:32.350 --> 00:50:32.630
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1187
00:50:32.770 --> 00:50:34.010
And Angela's eating this cookie.
安吉拉正在吃那块饼干。

1188
00:50:34.290 --> 00:50:35.510
She spits it out.
她把它吐了出来。

1189
00:50:35.790 --> 00:50:36.030
Yeah.
没错。

1190
00:50:36.030 --> 00:50:37.810
We did a lot of takes of this.
这一段我们拍了很多遍。

1191
00:50:37.930 --> 00:50:38.910
I'm not sure why.
我不确定为什么。

1192
00:50:39.090 --> 00:50:39.410
Okay.
好的。

1193
00:50:39.850 --> 00:50:43.770
But the cookie started to turn on me because I took a big bite.
但那块饼干开始让我难受了，因为我咬了一大口。

1194
00:50:43.910 --> 00:50:44.230
Okay.
好的。

1195
00:50:44.870 --> 00:50:45.350
Mistake.
失误。

1196
00:50:45.670 --> 00:50:45.910
Okay.
好的。

1197
00:50:46.050 --> 00:50:47.130
Take a small bite, guys.
伙计们，咬小口一点。

1198
00:50:47.330 --> 00:50:47.630
Always.
一定要这样。

1199
00:50:47.910 --> 00:50:48.230
Always.
一定要。

1200
00:50:48.570 --> 00:50:52.830
Because by the eighth take, the thought of that cookie makes you want to barf.
因为拍到第八遍的时候，一想到那块饼干就让你想吐。

1201
00:50:52.990 --> 00:50:53.210
Right.
没错。

1202
00:50:53.770 --> 00:50:55.210
It doesn't matter what it is.
不管那是什么都无所谓。

1203
00:50:55.250 --> 00:50:57.410
It doesn't matter if it's your favorite dessert.
哪怕是你最爱的甜点也一样。

1204
00:50:57.750 --> 00:50:58.030
Mm-mm.
嗯嗯。

1205
00:50:58.490 --> 00:51:00.310
And it started to turn on me.
它开始让我感到反胃了。

1206
00:51:00.390 --> 00:51:04.950
And so I took some peanuts and I stuck them in my hand.
所以我抓了一把花生放在手里。

1207
00:51:05.590 --> 00:51:10.110
And when they would cut to me eating, I would like just put a bunch of the peanuts in my mouth
当镜头切到我吃东西时，我就往嘴里塞一大把花生，

1208
00:51:10.110 --> 00:51:10.910
and hold the cookie.
然后手里拿着饼干。

1209
00:51:11.250 --> 00:51:13.010
I was trying to do a fakie eat.
我当时在尝试假吃。

1210
00:51:13.310 --> 00:51:14.410
Mm, fakie eat.
嗯，假吃。

1211
00:51:14.470 --> 00:51:14.890
Fakie eat.
假吃。

1212
00:51:14.990 --> 00:51:17.190
And then I would spit out peanuts instead of the cookie.
然后我就把花生吐出来，而不是饼干。

1213
00:51:17.190 --> 00:51:17.710
Okay.
好吧。

1214
00:51:18.070 --> 00:51:21.050
So what we see on camera, that is chewed up peanuts?
所以我们在镜头里看到的，其实是嚼碎的花生？

1215
00:51:21.410 --> 00:51:22.270
We don't know.
我们不知道。

1216
00:51:22.430 --> 00:51:23.510
We don't know which take they used.
我们不知道他们用了哪一条拍摄素材。

1217
00:51:23.510 --> 00:51:24.530
We don't know which take they used.
我们不知道他们用了哪一条拍摄素材。

1218
00:51:24.530 --> 00:51:25.170
Was it early?
是早期的吗？

1219
00:51:25.250 --> 00:51:25.770
Was it late?
还是后期的？

1220
00:51:25.890 --> 00:51:26.450
I don't know.
我不知道。

1221
00:51:26.630 --> 00:51:29.170
These are the things you try to do at work.
这些就是你在工作中会尝试做的事情。

1222
00:51:29.250 --> 00:51:30.890
How do I not eat that cookie?
我该怎么做才能不吃掉那块饼干呢？

1223
00:51:31.210 --> 00:51:35.290
Well, when Michael leaves his office with Meredith, they're going somewhere.
嗯，当迈克尔和梅雷迪思离开办公室时，他们要去某个地方。

1224
00:51:35.590 --> 00:51:35.930
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1225
00:51:35.930 --> 00:51:37.650
He says, I'll meet you in the parking lot.
他说，我在停车场等你。

1226
00:51:37.650 --> 00:51:42.050
And then he asks Toby for the number of that rehabilitation center.
然后他向托比要了那家康复中心的电话号码。

1227
00:51:42.370 --> 00:51:45.690
And everyone's like, wow, he did it.
大家都觉得，哇，他真的做到了。

1228
00:51:45.890 --> 00:51:46.290
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1229
00:51:46.290 --> 00:51:52.650
And then, you know, he finishes writing the number down and he throws the pen at Toby's
然后，你知道，他写完号码，就把笔扔向托比的

1230
00:51:52.650 --> 00:51:53.090
head.
头。

1231
00:51:53.230 --> 00:51:54.450
And hits him in the forehead.
正好砸在他的额头上。

1232
00:51:54.770 --> 00:51:56.910
We got a fan question about that.
我们收到一个粉丝关于此事的提问。

1233
00:51:57.130 --> 00:51:58.850
Well, we have stories about it, too.
其实我们也有关于这件事的故事。

1234
00:52:00.590 --> 00:52:05.630
Kelsey B would like to know, was the pen throwing scripted or improvised?
凯尔西·B想知道，扔笔这一幕是剧本写的还是即兴发挥的？

1235
00:52:06.490 --> 00:52:07.830
It was scripted.
是剧本写的。

1236
00:52:08.230 --> 00:52:12.850
And Justin said that Steve had a special rubber pen.
贾斯汀说史蒂夫有一支特制的橡胶笔。

1237
00:52:12.850 --> 00:52:18.870
And I remember it because it was in the pen cup on Pam's desk.
我记得很清楚，因为它当时就在帕姆桌上的笔筒里。

1238
00:52:19.090 --> 00:52:22.370
There were real pens and then one fakie pen.
里面有真笔，还有一支假笔。

1239
00:52:22.590 --> 00:52:22.890
Yeah.
没错。

1240
00:52:22.970 --> 00:52:29.870
And I was sitting there and I kept, like, positioning the pen so that Steve could pick up the fakie
我当时坐在那儿，一直调整笔的位置，好让史蒂夫能拿到那支假

1241
00:52:29.870 --> 00:52:30.210
pen.
笔。

1242
00:52:30.210 --> 00:52:34.370
This would have been another thing Phil Shea would have had to have gotten for the episode.
这又是菲尔·谢伊为了这一集必须准备的东西。

1243
00:52:34.950 --> 00:52:38.930
Fakie rubber pen so that he could throw it at Toby's head.
假橡胶笔，这样他才能把它扔向托比的头。

1244
00:52:39.090 --> 00:52:41.270
They inserted that little thump sound later.
那个“砰”的一声是后期加上去的。

1245
00:52:41.630 --> 00:52:43.910
We did about four or five takes of it, I guess.
我想我们大概拍了四五条吧。

1246
00:52:44.590 --> 00:52:49.030
You guys, if you rewatch this, you will notice behind Michael, there are no people.
各位，如果你们重看这一段，会发现迈克尔身后没有人。

1247
00:52:49.030 --> 00:52:52.030
We're all standing way off to the right.
我们都站在右侧很远的地方。

1248
00:52:52.210 --> 00:52:52.510
Yep.
没错。

1249
00:52:52.830 --> 00:52:53.550
You want to know why?
想知道为什么吗？

1250
00:52:53.770 --> 00:52:55.070
Because we couldn't stop laughing.
因为我们当时根本停不下来笑。

1251
00:52:55.270 --> 00:53:00.350
So when they would cut to Michael, after throwing it, we'd be behind him giggling.
所以当镜头切到迈克尔时，在他扔出笔之后，我们就在他身后偷笑。

1252
00:53:00.670 --> 00:53:00.810
Yep.
没错。

1253
00:53:00.830 --> 00:53:02.610
So they pushed us all to the right.
所以他们把我们都推到了右边。

1254
00:53:02.650 --> 00:53:07.510
And they had to get our reaction take like a whole beat later when we had gotten our composure.
而且他们不得不等我们平复心情后，再专门补拍我们的反应镜头。

1255
00:53:07.990 --> 00:53:09.790
Paul also couldn't stop laughing.
保罗也一直笑个不停。

1256
00:53:10.010 --> 00:53:10.550
I know.
我知道。

1257
00:53:10.750 --> 00:53:14.390
Every time that little rubber pen thumped him in the forehead, he would break.
每次那支橡胶笔弹到他额头上，他就会笑场。

1258
00:53:14.390 --> 00:53:15.210
I know.
我知道。

1259
00:53:15.210 --> 00:53:22.070
And there is such a fun blooper where Paul decided to prank Steve during this scene.
有一个特别有趣的NG片段，保罗决定在那场戏里捉弄史蒂夫。

1260
00:53:22.250 --> 00:53:23.350
We have to listen to it.
我们得听听看。

1261
00:53:24.650 --> 00:53:28.810
You know, could you write down the name of that rehabilitation clinic you mentioned?
那个，你能把刚才提到的那家康复诊所的名字写下来吗？

1262
00:53:29.390 --> 00:53:29.670
Wow.
哇。

1263
00:53:30.210 --> 00:53:30.350
Yeah.
是啊。

1264
00:53:35.420 --> 00:53:36.060
Impressive.
令人印象深刻。

1265
00:53:36.380 --> 00:53:36.860
That's great.
太棒了。

1266
00:53:38.280 --> 00:53:39.580
What does that even say?
那上面到底写了什么？

1267
