01:00:24.880 --> 01:00:30.800
making you feel put upon and all of this stuff, you can't constantly keep getting sad.
让你感到受气，诸如此类，你不可能一直让自己难过。

1416
01:00:30.800 --> 01:00:36.060
So it ended up being a very, very wonderful choice that I think he made.
所以最终这成了一个非常、非常棒的选择，我认为是他做出的。

1417
01:00:36.160 --> 01:00:40.720
But in the moment, I think he pretty much decided he wasn't going to act because he didn't want
但在那一刻，我想他基本上决定不去演，因为他不想

1418
01:00:40.720 --> 01:00:41.760
to be sad that day.
在那天感到难过。

1419
01:00:41.880 --> 01:00:43.280
And I'll never forget that.
我永远不会忘记这一点。

1420
01:00:43.480 --> 01:00:44.080
I loved it.
我太喜欢了。

1421
01:00:44.940 --> 01:00:47.100
Jen was so excited to tell me this story.
珍当时特别兴奋地跟我讲了这个故事。

1422
01:00:47.380 --> 01:00:49.900
She was like, I have to give him grief.
她说，我一定要好好损他一下。

1423
01:00:49.900 --> 01:00:53.600
And I guess they talked together and they were laughing about it.
我想他们当时聊过，还为此笑了很久。

1424
01:00:53.660 --> 01:00:55.200
And Paul was like, yeah, you can share.
保罗说，行啊，你可以分享。

1425
01:00:55.320 --> 01:00:56.380
You can share that.
你可以分享这个。

1426
01:00:56.540 --> 01:00:57.160
It's true.
这是真的。

1427
01:00:57.160 --> 01:00:58.520
I don't want to be sad.
我不想难过。

1428
01:00:58.740 --> 01:01:03.460
I don't want to dig too deep and actually cry in this scene because then I'm going to
我不想挖得太深，在这场戏里真的哭出来，因为那样的话我

1429
01:01:03.460 --> 01:01:04.340
be sad all day.
一整天都会很难过。

1430
01:01:04.540 --> 01:01:07.520
I'm going to be thinking about whatever precipitated it.
我会一直想着引发我难过的事情。

1431
01:01:07.780 --> 01:01:11.040
I love that Jen just wanted to give Paul s*** on our podcaSt.
我喜欢珍只是想在我们的播客上损保罗这一点。

1432
01:01:11.220 --> 01:01:11.660
I know.
我知道。

1433
01:01:11.880 --> 01:01:14.740
She was just like, email hits my inbox.
她当时就是，邮件发到了我的收件箱里。

1434
01:01:15.840 --> 01:01:17.120
Oh, so funny.
噢，太搞笑了。

1435
01:01:17.380 --> 01:01:21.340
I agree, though, when I watched the scene, like I didn't think anything of it.
不过我同意，当我看那场戏时，我没觉得有什么不对劲。

1436
01:01:21.480 --> 01:01:22.780
I was like, oh, that's perfect.
我当时想，噢，那太完美了。

1437
01:01:23.240 --> 01:01:23.480
Yeah.
是啊。

1438
01:01:24.140 --> 01:01:25.280
Oh, so funny.
噢，太搞笑了。

1439
01:01:25.280 --> 01:01:29.960
And I guess she would, like, give him shiitake about that for years to come.
我想她之后几年肯定会一直拿这事儿损他。

1440
01:01:31.000 --> 01:01:34.860
Gosh, speaking of sad, should we talk about the saddest scene ever?
天哪，说到悲伤，我们要不要聊聊史上最悲伤的一场戏？

1441
01:01:35.120 --> 01:01:36.160
Saddest scene ever.
史上最悲伤的戏。

1442
01:01:36.160 --> 01:01:38.760
It all starts because Angela is done.
这一切的起因是安吉拉受够了。

1443
01:01:39.040 --> 01:01:41.000
She is done with Phyllis.
她受够了菲利斯。

1444
01:01:41.120 --> 01:01:44.300
Well, Phyllis tells her to go get the tree and bring it back.
嗯，菲利斯让她去把树拿回来。

1445
01:01:44.460 --> 01:01:45.300
I know.
我知道。

1446
01:01:45.620 --> 01:01:47.880
Phyllis and I absolutely loved this episode.
菲利斯和我绝对爱死这一集了。

1447
01:01:48.080 --> 01:01:51.800
We got to do so much together, even more than you even see in the actual episode.
我们有很多对手戏，甚至比你在正片里看到的还要多。

1448
01:01:51.800 --> 01:02:00.200
I can't tell you how amazing it felt as Angela Martin to turn to her and say, shut up.
我无法形容作为安吉拉·马丁转过身对她说“闭嘴”时，那种感觉有多爽。

1449
01:02:01.500 --> 01:02:03.720
It felt so good.
感觉太棒了。

1450
01:02:04.020 --> 01:02:07.200
And I was really proud of this scene.
我真的为这场戏感到自豪。

1451
01:02:07.360 --> 01:02:12.260
I thought Phyllis and I really had this perfect chemistry in this moment.
我当时觉得菲利斯和我之间真的有一种完美的化学反应。

1452
01:02:12.260 --> 01:02:19.360
And then she tells everyone and she shames Angela Martin in front of the whole bullpen.
然后她告诉了所有人，还在整个办公区面前让安吉拉·马丁难堪。

1453
01:02:19.560 --> 01:02:25.980
And when she did, I was so in the moment with her, I felt the heat of my skin.
当她这么做的时候，我完全沉浸在当时的情境中，我甚至能感觉到皮肤在发烫。

1454
01:02:26.220 --> 01:02:28.460
Like my face started to flush.
就像我的脸开始泛红一样。

1455
01:02:28.680 --> 01:02:28.880
Yeah.
没错。

1456
01:02:29.040 --> 01:02:30.060
You can see it.
你能看出来的。

1457
01:02:30.060 --> 01:02:32.360
Everyone is looking at you.
每个人都在看着你。

1458
01:02:32.840 --> 01:02:33.360
Everyone.
所有人。

1459
01:02:33.760 --> 01:02:39.260
You know, and we've talked about whenever you had a scene where the whole bullpen focused on you,
你知道，我们之前聊过，每当你有一场戏是整个办公区的人都盯着你看的时候，

1460
01:02:39.460 --> 01:02:42.400
you were already heightened a little bit like your nerves.
你当时的情绪已经有点紧绷了，就像你的神经一样。

1461
01:02:42.760 --> 01:02:50.480
And I really just, oh man, I was, as the character, I felt like I couldn't get out of there fast enough.
我真的，天哪，作为角色本身，我当时觉得我恨不得立刻逃离那里。

1462
01:02:51.260 --> 01:02:54.040
And then Andy walks in.
然后安迪走了进来。

1463
01:02:54.280 --> 01:02:55.160
I know.
我知道。

1464
01:02:55.560 --> 01:03:07.380
And the way Ed just, you know, Ed Helms, the person, his inherent goodness and sweetheart just carries through the character of Andy.
还有艾德，你知道的，艾德·赫尔姆斯本人，他那种与生俱来的善良和甜美，完全融入了安迪这个角色。

1465
01:03:07.700 --> 01:03:08.360
I know.
我知道。

1466
01:03:08.480 --> 01:03:09.380
Well, here's the thing.
嗯，问题是这样的。

1467
01:03:09.600 --> 01:03:13.080
Is Andy like completely annoying?
安迪是不是特别烦人？

1468
01:03:13.500 --> 01:03:13.820
Sure.
当然。

1469
01:03:14.140 --> 01:03:14.560
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

1470
01:03:14.740 --> 01:03:17.020
But he's also got this boyish charm.
但他身上也有一种孩子气的魅力。

1471
01:03:17.260 --> 01:03:17.460
Yeah.
没错。

1472
01:03:17.680 --> 01:03:19.820
A boyish enthusiasm, right?
一种孩子气的热情，对吧？

1473
01:03:19.820 --> 01:03:20.260
Yes.
是的。

1474
01:03:20.580 --> 01:03:22.380
For singing this song to you.
为了给你唱这首歌。

1475
01:03:22.580 --> 01:03:23.040
Yes.
是的。

1476
01:03:23.240 --> 01:03:27.280
And in the script, the song he sings is Silent Night.
剧本里他唱的歌是《平安夜》。

1477
01:03:27.880 --> 01:03:29.580
Oh, yes.
哦，对。

1478
01:03:29.980 --> 01:03:30.300
Mm-hmm.
嗯嗯。

1479
01:03:30.620 --> 01:03:36.940
Randy said the morning of the shoot, they told Ed he was so scared to say it.
兰迪说拍摄当天早上，他们告诉艾德的时候，他特别紧张。

1480
01:03:37.040 --> 01:03:39.100
He said they've changed their mind.
他说他们改变主意了。

1481
01:03:39.280 --> 01:03:40.980
Can you do Deck the Halls?
你能唱《装饰大厅》吗？

1482
01:03:41.100 --> 01:03:44.460
Ed had to learn a whole new song to play on the sitar.
艾德得现学一首新歌用西塔琴弹奏。

1483
01:03:44.640 --> 01:03:46.320
He had just learned Silent Night.
他刚学会《平安夜》。

1484
01:03:46.320 --> 01:03:50.380
Yes, he'd had that thing for a couple weeks and he'd been fiddling around on it.
是的，他练那首歌练了好几周，一直在上面拨弄。

1485
01:03:50.500 --> 01:03:52.520
And then they were like, can you do Deck the Halls?
然后他们突然说，你能弹《装饰大厅》吗？

1486
01:03:52.660 --> 01:03:57.120
Randy told me it took him about a minute and a half to figure it out because he's amazing.
兰迪告诉我，他只花了一分半钟就搞定了，因为他太厉害了。

1487
01:03:57.300 --> 01:03:58.120
Yeah, he's a musical genius.
没错，他是个音乐天才。

1488
01:03:58.700 --> 01:04:07.260
They thought it would be funny, the juxtaposition of this sort of very cringey moment for Andy to be playing this upbeat song.
他们觉得这样会很有趣，安迪在那种极其尴尬的时刻弹奏这首欢快的歌，这种反差感。

1489
01:04:07.260 --> 01:04:10.920
And you know he improvised the Riddity to-do at the end?
而且你知道结尾那个“Riddity to-do”是他即兴发挥的吗？

1490
01:04:11.020 --> 01:04:11.560
I know.
我知道。

1491
01:04:11.640 --> 01:04:12.300
So good.
太棒了。

1492
01:04:12.680 --> 01:04:14.880
We're all just staring at him.
我们当时都盯着他看。

1493
01:04:15.040 --> 01:04:17.260
And Ed played the moment so perfectly.
艾德把那一刻演得太完美了。

1494
01:04:17.720 --> 01:04:20.280
My heart completely broke for Andy.
我当时真的为安迪感到心碎。

1495
01:04:20.340 --> 01:04:23.840
I felt so bad for him and I started to cry.
我为他感到难过，甚至开始哭了。

1496
01:04:24.060 --> 01:04:25.400
Like actually crying?
是真哭吗？

1497
01:04:25.660 --> 01:04:25.900
Yeah.
是的。

1498
01:04:26.380 --> 01:04:27.940
I actually cry.
我是真的哭了。

1499
01:04:28.100 --> 01:04:33.600
If you look at this, it pushes it on my face and I'm completely tearing up.
如果你仔细看，镜头推到我脸上时，我确实在流泪。

1500
01:04:33.600 --> 01:04:45.060
Those are those moments as an actor where you have so inhabited your character's story and the story of the people around you where your body,
作为演员，当你完全沉浸在角色的故事以及周围人的故事中时，你的身体就会出现那种时刻，

1501
01:04:45.260 --> 01:04:48.680
like you didn't even have to make yourself cry or think of something sad.
就好像你根本不需要强迫自己哭，也不用去想什么伤心事。

1502
01:04:48.680 --> 01:04:52.780
You were just so in the moment that the emotions just flood.
你当时完全沉浸在情境中，情绪自然而然地就涌出来了。

1503
01:04:53.060 --> 01:04:54.360
No, really, really.
真的，真的。

1504
01:04:54.500 --> 01:04:56.900
And everyone was playing it so real.
而且每个人的表演都非常真实。

1505
01:04:57.540 --> 01:04:59.100
Paul Feig told us to.
是保罗·费格让我们这么做的。

1506
01:04:59.320 --> 01:05:05.560
Like he said when we come around with that B camera, and this was similar to his direction in Office Olympics, he said,
就像他说的那样，当我们带着B机位靠近时，这和他在《办公室奥运会》里的指导很像，他说，

1507
01:05:05.740 --> 01:05:10.400
I don't want you to comment on it with no kind of funny looks or anything.
我不希望你们对此做出任何评价，也不要露出任何滑稽的表情之类的。

1508
01:05:10.720 --> 01:05:14.600
Like this is like truly a human moment.
这就像是一个真正的人性时刻。

1509
01:05:14.940 --> 01:05:16.360
And just stand there.
就站在那里。

1510
01:05:16.540 --> 01:05:17.800
Just be in it.
身临其境就好。

1511
01:05:18.280 --> 01:05:19.700
It was great direction.
这指导太棒了。

1512
01:05:20.120 --> 01:05:21.180
And you felt it.
而且你确实感受到了。

1513
01:05:21.300 --> 01:05:21.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1514
01:05:21.860 --> 01:05:22.880
It felt heavy.
感觉很沉重。

1515
01:05:23.140 --> 01:05:24.200
It felt really heavy.
感觉真的非常沉重。

1516
01:05:24.200 --> 01:05:26.560
And I felt horrible.
我当时感觉糟透了。

1517
01:05:27.220 --> 01:05:28.720
And I started to cry.
然后我就开始哭了。

1518
01:05:29.300 --> 01:05:37.480
You know, in re-watching it all, I just thought this episode was written and directed and acted so, so well.
你知道吗，在重温这一切时，我只是觉得这一集的剧本、导演和表演都太出色了。

1519
01:05:37.660 --> 01:05:39.280
I was really proud of us as a show.
我真的为我们这部剧感到自豪。

1520
01:05:39.460 --> 01:05:40.480
You know what, Angela?
你知道吗，安吉拉？

1521
01:05:40.720 --> 01:05:43.400
This was what Paul Feig could do for us.
这就是保罗·费格能为我们做到的。

1522
01:05:43.620 --> 01:05:51.420
You know, like he was really good at directing us to allow these moments to breathe.
你知道，他非常擅长指导我们，让我们有空间去沉淀这些时刻。

1523
01:05:51.420 --> 01:05:52.880
And you're so good in this.
而且你在这集里表现得太棒了。

1524
01:05:53.040 --> 01:05:53.860
Oh, thanks, lady.
噢，谢谢你，亲爱的。

1525
01:05:53.860 --> 01:05:57.600
You're so good in this whole episode and this moment at the end.
你在整集以及最后那个时刻的表现都太好了。

1526
01:05:57.920 --> 01:06:01.520
It is more powerful because it's real.
正因为它真实，所以才更有感染力。

1527
01:06:01.980 --> 01:06:02.320
Yeah.
没错。

1528
01:06:02.580 --> 01:06:03.620
You really nailed it.
你真的演得太到位了。

1529
01:06:03.780 --> 01:06:05.020
Thanks so much, lady.
太感谢了，亲爱的。

1530
01:06:05.260 --> 01:06:05.780
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1531
01:06:05.980 --> 01:06:09.440
And I thought Kate Flannery crushed this episode too.
我觉得凯特·弗兰纳里在这一集里也表现得非常出彩。

1532
01:06:09.660 --> 01:06:09.880
Same.
我也是这么觉得。

1533
01:06:09.880 --> 01:06:15.640
And you know, guys, the supporting cast, these moments were fewer and far between for us.
而且你们知道吗，伙计们，对于我们这些配角来说，这样的时刻并不多见。

1534
01:06:15.700 --> 01:06:18.280
And so when they happened, we just treasured it.
所以当它们出现时，我们都倍加珍惜。

1535
01:06:18.380 --> 01:06:20.520
And it was so fun to re-watch it.
重温这一集真的太有趣了。

1536
01:06:20.880 --> 01:06:28.560
And you guys would get these scripts with no notice and you'd have to just step up to the plate and suddenly carry an episode.
你们总是会毫无预兆地拿到剧本，然后就得挺身而出，突然挑起一整集的大梁。

1537
01:06:28.960 --> 01:06:33.400
And you always did it because we had a really great bench on our show.
但你们总是能做到，因为我们的剧组有着非常强大的替补阵容。

1538
01:06:33.540 --> 01:06:34.900
We had a deep bench, y'all.
我们有着深厚的板凳深度，伙计们。

1539
01:06:34.980 --> 01:06:35.460
We did.
确实如此。

1540
01:06:35.460 --> 01:06:38.480
Well, that is Moroccan Christmas.
好了，这就是《摩洛哥圣诞节》。

1541
01:06:38.880 --> 01:06:39.660
We did it.
我们做到了。

1542
01:06:39.760 --> 01:06:40.480
We did it.
我们做到了。

1543
01:06:40.600 --> 01:06:44.020
We all hope you'll have a little responsabilitini in your life.
我们都希望你们的生活中也能有一点“责任马提尼”。

1544
01:06:44.300 --> 01:06:44.700
Yeah.
没错。

1545
01:06:44.920 --> 01:06:54.720
And just want to give a few thank yous to Justin Spitzer, Erin Schur, Halstead Sullivan, Jen Salata, Randy Cordray, and Stephen Sox.
还要特别感谢贾斯汀·斯皮策、艾琳·舒尔、霍尔斯特德·沙利文、詹·萨拉塔、兰迪·科德雷和斯蒂芬·索克斯。

1546
01:06:54.880 --> 01:06:59.520
Remember, you can find Stephen and his wife, Lori, on their podcast if we knew then.
记住，你们可以在斯蒂芬和他的妻子洛瑞的播客《如果我们当时知道》中找到他们。

1547
01:06:59.680 --> 01:07:02.820
And I know you traded a bunch of messages with Kate as well, Angela.
而且我知道你和凯特也交换了很多信息，安吉拉。

1548
01:07:02.820 --> 01:07:08.360
Kate Flannery and James Carey because the script having the shooting draft was just amazing for this one.
凯特·弗兰纳里和詹姆斯·凯里，因为这一集的拍摄剧本简直太棒了。

1549
01:07:08.640 --> 01:07:15.140
And before we go, one little tidbit we're so excited to finally get to share with you.
在结束之前，还有一个我们终于可以和大家分享的小花絮。

1550
01:07:15.180 --> 01:07:15.740
Yes.
是的。

1551
01:07:15.880 --> 01:07:23.940
We're so excited to tell you guys that we have partnered with Comedy Central and Cartooner Radio to bring you animated clips of our podcaSt.
我们非常激动地告诉大家，我们已经与喜剧中心频道和Cartooner Radio达成合作，将为我们的播客制作动画短片。

1552
01:07:24.360 --> 01:07:24.780
Yes.
没错。

1553
01:07:25.040 --> 01:07:29.560
You know, we're constantly getting mail from people saying they wish they could watch us on video.
你们知道，我们经常收到听众来信，说他们希望能看到我们的视频。

1554
01:07:29.560 --> 01:07:35.260
And for many reasons we won't get into now, we do not videotape our podcaSt.
出于一些我们现在不便详述的原因，我们并没有录制播客视频。

1555
01:07:36.380 --> 01:07:44.920
But Cartooner Radio has taken some of the audio and they have animated it, which in my opinion is even better than watching a video.
但Cartooner Radio选取了一些音频并将其制作成了动画，在我看来，这甚至比看视频还要棒。

1556
01:07:45.160 --> 01:07:46.020
It is, you guys.
确实如此，伙计们。

1557
01:07:46.160 --> 01:07:47.360
They are so creative.
他们太有创意了。

1558
01:07:47.560 --> 01:07:48.900
Jenna and I are now a cartoon.
珍娜和我现在成了卡通人物。

1559
01:07:49.620 --> 01:07:50.700
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1560
01:07:50.780 --> 01:07:51.340
I love it.
我太喜欢了。

1561
01:07:51.340 --> 01:07:53.960
